Spoilers Ahead

When there's a will, there's generally a way.  Medusa can be bypassed by
using a pickaxe (mug a dwarf) to dig down to the next level.  While a
cloak of magic resistance is useful, and gray dragon scale mail is better,
you really NEED them til you meet the Wiz (but you better have one then
or "finger of death" will get you).  This means that you can get that
from the WOW in the stronghold.  Excalibur is a reasonable weapon that
you can almost certainly get without too much trouble.  A shield or
amulet of reflection is convenient but not essential.  Watch out for
Blackie the dragon, stay off-line, move next to him, he'll bite but
not breathe (very accomodating).  Kill him and eat him, repeat this
til you feel very firm.  Same sort of strategy for other missing
intrinsics - after a while, who needs reflection ?

Oh yeah, don't forget about Medusa on the way up!  

If you still don't have a blindfold, here are other ideas, either for
the way down, or back up.   You can blind yourself with a
potion of blindness, wand of lightning (engrave with it),
cursed unicorn horn, blessed OR cursed scroll of create monster (create
a yellow light).
If you on the way back up, and you had to use all of your wishes,
then put the amulet down, level teleport to a level where you had
found a magic trap, step into that till you get blinded,
then level teleport back to nail Medusa.  Or go rob a shop, and let
the Kops hit you with a cream pie.

If you have stealth and a wand of cancellation, sneak up on her and
zap her with the wand, the kill her slowly.

And...for the #1 fun way to do her in: polymorph yourself into an
ochre jelly or a yellow dragon.

Anyway, I actually did have to dig past Medusa one game, but I found
a blindfold out of the stash in Vlad's tower, and destroyed her on the
way out.  Just don't forget...

