I have decided that there is no one item that is "theoretically"
necessary to win the game (except the amulet!).  In practice, I have
never won without speed boots - but then again I've never tried.
They are by far the most powerful item in the game.  Other than that,
I've won in a variety of ways, some more elegant than others.
The most artistic involves a -1 Stormy, stethoscope, and polymorph
control, where I don't ever kill the Wiz, just reduce him to a
pipsqueak and steal his most cherished possession.  This strategy
was suggested by Dave Hairston.  The crudest is the old cockatrice
corpse in the ice-box trick.  The run-of-the mill method is smashing
him flat with a +8 Mjollnir every time he resurrects.

As I said earlier though, it is ALMOST necessary to have either a cloak
of magic resistance, or a gray dragon scale mail.  If not, better use
the cockatrice corpse and don't dawdle.

